\begin{block}{A standard analysis workflow has the following steps:}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Find the most correlated and anticorrelated genes.
\item Find the features that show highest variance between these correlated/anticorrelated candidates.
\item Use these feature to guide comparisons between perturbed cells and negative controls.
\item Fetch images for these perturbations for inspection
\item Retrieve additional annotations from existing databases.
\end{enumerate}
\end{block}
\begin{block}{We provide libraries for data scientists and developers}
We compare images using tools that decompose the channels to focus on the most important features obtained from data mining

Examples of these tools and other workflows are available on the JUMP Hub.
\end{block}
